WEBVTT

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:15.990
Blue eyes...

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.940
Do you know what this is?

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.290
That's...

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:30.800
...the Makiri I made for Asirpa.

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:33.090
Why do you have it?

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:35.510
So it was true.

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:41.170
Nopperabo really is Asirpa-san's father?

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:45.440
Is she... here?

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:46.230
Come with me!

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:48.130
You're telling me everything!

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:52.570
If you want to know where the 
gold is, bring Asirpa to me!

00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:54.520
I'll only tell my daughter!

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:02.040
<b>Episode Twenty-Four
Call Out</b>

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:02.040
<b>Chapel</b>

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:02.040
Enomoto Takeaki is now a viscount!

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:06.670
And Hijikata Toshizou is 
an aged, fugitive prisoner!

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:10.040
If you'd only agreed to join the 
new Meiji government's army...

00:01:12.310 --> 00:01:16.420
You wouldn't have spent more 
than thirty years in chains!

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:21.720
Beg for your life!

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.730
Obey me! Serve me!

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:28.230
Polish my boots every day, and do 
whatever it takes to keep me happy!

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:34.900
After all these years, you're still 
telling me to join the Meiji government?

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:39.690
You people in the new government 
returned the loyalty

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:42.470
shown to you by the Tokugawas with hatred,

00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:47.210
and yet now you demand 
loyalty from the people.

00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:50.680
You're scared.

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:56.790
The soldiers of the old shogunate who became 
martyrs scare you more than anything else.

00:01:57.970 --> 00:02:03.990
In order to justify your brother, 
who died in the Battle of Hakodate,

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:06.410
as well as your own life,

00:02:06.410 --> 00:02:11.570
you needed to lock me away 
until I became one of you.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:18.650
And when that moment comes, the revenge 
of Inudou Shirosuke will be complete!

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:21.620
Until this moment,

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:24.910
you've been unable to bear the fact 
that a peasant from the countryside

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:31.420
like me was more loyal than the samurai!

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:34.070
I'll make you obey me,

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:35.300
even if I have to cut off your limbs!

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:53.360
I'm still young enough to take you alive.

00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:16.000
Do it, last of the samurai.

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:28.850
You're going to tell me where the gold is,

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:33.150
but first, there's something I've wanted 
to say to you for a long time.

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:36.210
To tell you the truth,

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:39.190
I don't want Asirpa-san to see you!

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:44.450
She was terrified that the man who 
killed the Ainu and stole their gold

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:47.450
might really be her father.

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:51.960
Why did you tell Hijikata Toshizou 
the name Kochoube Asuko?

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:54.420
Why did you get Asirpa-san involved?

00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:58.340
To entrust her with the future.

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:00.520
I made it so Asirpa could 
hide in the mountains,

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:03.430
fighting as a guerrilla.

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:07.140
My daughter will be a leader of the Ainu.

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:11.150
Lead the Ainu?

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:15.350
You want to use her for an 
Ainu independence movement?

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:19.320
You want her to be the Ainu Jeanne d'Arc?

00:04:21.430 --> 00:04:22.820
What's wrong?

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:24.740
We haven't had enough fun here yet!

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:28.720
Come say hello to my friend here!

00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:35.080
You want to make her a murderer like us?

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:37.540
Sure, maybe what you're doing is right!

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:40.190
Maybe somebody has to fight!

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:44.760
But it doesn't... it doesn't have to be her!

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:48.810
I want Asirpa-san to hunt
deer in the mountains,

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:50.010
eat their brains,

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:51.540
turn them into chitatap,

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:54.020
and say, "Hinna, hinna!"

00:04:56.740 --> 00:05:01.230
That girl seems to have had 
quite an effect on you, Sisam.

00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:10.550
That kimono...

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:17.000
Red prisoner's clothes...

00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:18.920
And next to him...

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:21.630
Asirpa-chan, get up here!

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:27.800
Well? Can you see her?

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:30.260
Inkarmat...

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:35.910
Nopperabo must be close!

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:36.730
Find him!

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:39.640
Over there!

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:53.080
<i>Aca...</i>

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:55.790
It's a red-haired Kimun Kamuy.

00:05:56.470 --> 00:05:57.740
Asirpa...

00:05:57.740 --> 00:05:59.120
You defeat it.

00:06:01.270 --> 00:06:02.260
Aca?

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:38.210
The poison got it.

00:06:39.590 --> 00:06:41.480
Congratulations, Asirpa.

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:43.670
You didn't get scared,
and your movements were precise.

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:53.140
You're still so young, but you 
fought and defeated a bear!

00:06:55.030 --> 00:06:56.200
I'm sorry.

00:07:00.010 --> 00:07:01.700
I'm so proud of you, daughter.

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:03.590
Your mustache stinks.

00:07:06.770 --> 00:07:07.890
Asirpa...

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:10.020
My daughter.

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:13.910
You are the future of the Ainu.

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:19.420
Well, Asirpa?

00:07:19.420 --> 00:07:21.080
Is that your father?

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:24.080
Well?

00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:27.000
It's Aca.

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:30.090
You're sure that's Wilk?

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:33.550
What's the look on her face?

00:07:43.670 --> 00:07:44.550
<i>Aca...</i>

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:46.710
<i>Why?</i>

00:07:55.430 --> 00:07:58.160
I wasn't the one who killed the Ainu.

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:02.250
Tell Asirpa that.

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:02.920
The gold—

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:12.050
Wilk was shot!

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:33.860
Sugimoto!

00:08:40.930 --> 00:08:44.070
Asirpa-chan, run. Now.

00:08:44.070 --> 00:08:49.710
Now the only key to the mystery 
of the gold is within you.

00:08:50.490 --> 00:08:53.080
Everyone will start killing 
each other over you!

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:07.310
Aca! Sugimoto!

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:09.370
They're goners! Give up!

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:10.040
Let go of me! Let go!

00:09:09.370 --> 00:09:10.940
We're leaving, Asirpa!

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:13.670
I won't believe it! I won't leave them!

00:09:13.670 --> 00:09:16.160
Let me go! They're right there!

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:16.920
No!

00:09:16.460 --> 00:09:20.860
Let go! Aca! Sugimoto!

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:19.160
Whoever shot them is close!

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:22.530
Sugimoto? Seriously?

00:09:22.530 --> 00:09:23.620
What do we do?

00:09:25.640 --> 00:09:26.830
I'll go.

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:29.060
You stay close to Asirpa.

00:09:29.060 --> 00:09:30.420
Wait by the spare ship.

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:32.920
Tanigaki Nispa, don't go!

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:34.470
You'll be shot, too!

00:09:45.010 --> 00:09:47.390
A little further to the left, huh?

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:00.910
That goddamn Matagi...

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:27.810
<b>Abashiri
 Prison</b>

00:10:31.410 --> 00:10:32.770
Inkarmat!

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:37.610
What's wrong? What happened?

00:10:41.220 --> 00:10:44.740
When Wilk was shot...

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:52.830
Kiroranke gave a signal to someone.

00:10:53.650 --> 00:10:55.160
Kiroranke?

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:59.170
Private Tanigaki Genjirou...

00:11:04.580 --> 00:11:07.720
This is probably the spare ship.

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:09.770
Let's wait for everyone here.

00:11:13.930 --> 00:11:16.400
Huh? Where's Inkarmat-chan?

00:11:17.110 --> 00:11:22.530
You know why the 7th was able to 
find out everything we did, right?

00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:24.160
That woman's the only possible reason!

00:11:24.730 --> 00:11:26.830
We can't take her with us.

00:11:29.270 --> 00:11:30.490
Get the ship ready.

00:11:30.490 --> 00:11:31.500
We're leaving.

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:34.930
Tanigaki was caught by Lt. Tsurumi's men.

00:11:34.930 --> 00:11:36.450
And Aca and Sugimoto?

00:11:42.610 --> 00:11:46.470
I got close and looked, but both were dead.

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:14.040
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:12:28.730 --> 00:12:30.900
Immortal Sugimoto...

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:34.980
How does it feel to be 
missing part of your brain?

00:12:35.380 --> 00:12:38.470
We're brain damage pals now!

00:12:39.730 --> 00:12:43.360
I can't believe a murderer like
you was such a great doctor.

00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:47.190
They say there's a thin line between 
genius and insanity, but...

00:12:47.190 --> 00:12:52.240
I've done lots of cranial surgeries 
while pursuing my hobby of torture.

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:54.360
I would cut out their brains little by little,

00:12:54.360 --> 00:12:58.400
then fry and eat them in front of the 
victim while they were still conscious.

00:12:58.400 --> 00:12:59.780
With ginger soy sauce!

00:13:04.810 --> 00:13:08.300
Well, only someone like Sugimoto-san, 
with his incredible capacity for recovery,

00:13:08.300 --> 00:13:09.930
could've survived that.

00:13:10.580 --> 00:13:13.700
Inkarmat-san is the one who's in danger.

00:13:13.700 --> 00:13:16.440
If you want to learn anything 
from her, do it now.

00:13:17.140 --> 00:13:22.940
Kiroranke and his friends 
must've gone to Karafuto.

00:13:28.900 --> 00:13:30.660
We'll get on another ship at the port.

00:13:32.010 --> 00:13:33.370
Get a hold of yourself.

00:13:34.130 --> 00:13:36.370
Let's go, Asirpa.

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:42.000
The sound of the gun that 
shot Wilk and Sugimoto-san

00:13:42.650 --> 00:13:45.720
was covered up by the 
roar of the star shells.

00:13:46.210 --> 00:13:47.730
I didn't hear it.

00:13:48.760 --> 00:13:52.810
Only Ogata could fire a shot like that.

00:13:54.890 --> 00:13:58.480
I felt him when I was shot.

00:14:00.530 --> 00:14:03.830
Was there a need to shoot Sugimoto?

00:14:04.850 --> 00:14:08.500
Right after we learned that 
Nopperabo was her father,

00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:10.910
he and Sugimoto exchanged words.

00:14:11.440 --> 00:14:14.400
Whether it was the location of the gold,

00:14:14.400 --> 00:14:16.500
or the key to cracking some 
code only Asirpa knows...

00:14:16.890 --> 00:14:19.960
Or perhaps it was about you?

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:25.020
He might be alive, you know.

00:14:25.020 --> 00:14:26.630
With Asirpa taken from him,

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:30.390
Immortal Sugimoto is 
probably real pissed off.

00:14:31.650 --> 00:14:34.890
I'll murder Ogata and Kiroranke both.

00:14:34.890 --> 00:14:38.970
Henmi Kazuo, Nihei Tetsuzou...

00:14:39.490 --> 00:14:42.710
You did a good job of catching them.

00:14:42.710 --> 00:14:47.360
So what proves that Kiroranke's 
group made it to Karafuto?

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:50.570
Wait!

00:14:50.570 --> 00:14:52.420
I just saw you on the roof—

00:14:52.420 --> 00:14:53.910
Take Asirpa!

00:14:54.260 --> 00:14:56.120
This woman is dangerous!

00:14:56.120 --> 00:14:58.110
Don't believe him, Asirpa-chan!

00:14:58.110 --> 00:14:59.370
Kiroranke just...

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:01.640
Shut up!

00:15:03.400 --> 00:15:05.190
You'll pay for what you did to Wilk!

00:15:16.630 --> 00:15:17.890
I didn't mean to stab—

00:15:21.850 --> 00:15:23.190
Let go!

00:15:26.810 --> 00:15:30.780
If we don't do something, the bigger 
countries will just swallow us up!

00:15:31.120 --> 00:15:36.240
Why did Wilk have to die?

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:39.570
Because he changed!

00:15:40.420 --> 00:15:44.500
The plan was to tell our old 
comrades where the gold was!

00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:47.920
<b>Abashiri
 Prison</b>

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:53.450
After killing the seven Ainu,
Nopperabo took a small amount of the gold

00:15:53.450 --> 00:15:56.260
and headed to Karafuto.
 He was captured on the way.

00:15:56.260 --> 00:15:58.590
I think he was carrying 
reliable information with him.

00:15:58.590 --> 00:16:01.770
He was planning to bring in their main force.

00:16:02.360 --> 00:16:05.810
With Asirpa, the critical key,
 in his possession,

00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:12.030
Kiroranke will probably try to meet up with 
his former guerrilla friends in the far east.

00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:16.310
If those partisans get their hands 
on Asirpa, we'll have a problem.

00:16:17.090 --> 00:16:19.580
I'll get her back!

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:21.650
Take me to Karafuto.

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:25.840
Without me, she won't trust you.

00:16:25.840 --> 00:16:27.460
I'll go, too.

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:31.540
Asirpa trusts us and nobody else.

00:16:31.540 --> 00:16:32.600
You're sure?

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:35.590
I'll come back, I promise.

00:16:36.090 --> 00:16:37.660
Stay alive until then.

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:39.350
I'll never forgive you if you die.

00:16:41.140 --> 00:16:44.130
Bring back Asirpa-san, please!

00:16:44.130 --> 00:16:46.270
Asirpa-san!

00:16:46.270 --> 00:16:49.270
You ate some of my brains, didn't you?

00:16:49.590 --> 00:16:55.890
I still have clean-up work to do 
at Abashiri, so I can't leave yet.

00:16:56.370 --> 00:16:59.740
For now, we're going to send a small 
force ahead of the rest of us.

00:17:00.470 --> 00:17:02.790
Sergeant Tsukishima, Lieutenant Koito...

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:04.890
You go with them!

00:17:07.940 --> 00:17:12.210
"Why do I have to leave you, 
Lt. Tsurumi?" he asks.

00:17:12.210 --> 00:17:15.590
It is a request from 
your father, Admiral Koito.

00:17:27.190 --> 00:17:32.850
<b>Chapel</b>

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:32.850
The 7th knew exactly what 
we were doing at Abashiri.

00:17:32.850 --> 00:17:37.200
That means Old Man Nagakura and the others 
at the kotan may have been captured.

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:40.840
In two or three days,
 things will calm down up there.

00:17:40.840 --> 00:17:42.700
And there'll be fewer soldiers in the area.

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:44.920
Just wait until then.

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:52.480
Did Inudou make this?

00:17:52.480 --> 00:17:59.550
It seems he was gathering information about
the escaped prisoners to lure me to Abashiri.

00:18:00.070 --> 00:18:03.770
Some of this is information we don't have.

00:18:03.770 --> 00:18:09.720
If the skins we had are now 
in Lt. Tsurumi's hands...

00:18:10.150 --> 00:18:13.780
We need to get at least one of the others 
so we can stop him from breaking the code.

00:18:14.490 --> 00:18:17.480
I thought Abashiri had turned 
out to be a waste of time,

00:18:17.480 --> 00:18:20.160
but at the very last moment, 
we found a glimmer of light.

00:18:21.480 --> 00:18:24.100
We're leaving here and going to the south!

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:40.710
Sugimoto-don...

00:18:43.690 --> 00:18:46.660
You want to send your kid on a journey, huh?

00:18:47.080 --> 00:18:50.420
He might not come back alive.

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:53.230
He's ready to die.

00:18:53.680 --> 00:18:57.440
My son will be a leader of men someday.

00:18:57.440 --> 00:19:01.780
And a leader has to take responsibility 
for many young lives.

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:08.040
I need him to be a man who's worthy of that.

00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:13.800
When Lieutenant General Hanazawa 
committed seppuku, he sent me a letter.

00:19:14.310 --> 00:19:18.310
His son, Yuusaku-don, 
had died on the front lines,

00:19:18.310 --> 00:19:21.270
upholding the honor of his foolish father.

00:19:22.280 --> 00:19:29.000
The war our generation started sent the 
sons of many of our citizens to battle.

00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:36.890
If I keep my own son from danger,
what can I say to those whose sons died?

00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:42.090
I think Nopperabo was the same way.

00:19:42.910 --> 00:19:46.480
He was telling the Ainu to die,

00:19:46.480 --> 00:19:50.910
so first, he had to send his 
own daughter into battle.

00:19:51.320 --> 00:19:56.880
He didn't raise her just to be used, I think.

00:20:07.910 --> 00:20:09.080
Sugimoto...

00:20:10.310 --> 00:20:11.350
Asirpa-san.

00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:13.410
Sugimoto...

00:20:13.850 --> 00:20:14.760
You're...

00:20:18.680 --> 00:20:22.040
I couldn't bring you to meet your father.

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:29.350
I'm sorry I couldn't keep my promise.

00:20:30.840 --> 00:20:34.830
Aca... left on his journey, then?

00:20:36.610 --> 00:20:37.790
I'm sorry.

00:20:41.010 --> 00:20:44.710
Just wait. I'll come for you.

00:20:44.710 --> 00:20:47.460
I swear I'll come for you!

00:20:51.970 --> 00:20:53.460
This is a dream.

00:20:54.130 --> 00:20:58.890
If the kamuy are trying to tell me something,
 there must be some meaning.

00:20:59.520 --> 00:21:00.440
No!

00:21:01.450 --> 00:21:04.470
Asirpa-san! It's not the 
kamuy that are speaking!

00:21:04.470 --> 00:21:05.570
It's me!

00:21:08.630 --> 00:21:13.640
I'm alive! And there's so 
much I want to tell you!

00:21:18.370 --> 00:21:20.920
What's wrong, Asirpa-chan?

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:34.600
I dreamed about Sugimoto.

00:21:36.410 --> 00:21:38.440
He said he was coming for me.

00:21:39.720 --> 00:21:41.760
That dream might be true.

00:21:41.760 --> 00:21:45.030
I just can't imagine him dying.

00:21:45.500 --> 00:21:47.210
What are you saying, Shiraishi?

00:21:47.210 --> 00:21:48.820
Of course he's not dead.

00:21:54.840 --> 00:21:56.960
Just wait, Asirpa-san...

00:21:58.050 --> 00:21:59.030
He's...

00:21:59.880 --> 00:22:00.880
I'm...

00:22:02.470 --> 00:22:04.120
...Immortal Sugimoto!
